---
// Three guardrail layers (context, execution, data) stacked in order of how hard each is to bypass.
---

<svg
	class="dg"
	viewBox="0 0 720 430"
	role="img"
	aria-labelledby="d-gl-title d-gl-desc"
	style="min-width: 630px"
>
	<title id="d-gl-title">Three guardrail layers, ordered by how hard they are to bypass</title>
	<desc id="d-gl-desc">
		Three stacked guardrail bands. At the top, the context layer governs what the model sees, with relevance and
		safety classifiers, moderation, rules, and source labels. In the middle, the execution layer governs what the model
		does, with tool risk rating, human confirmation, a PII filter, and output validation. At the bottom, the data layer
		governs what may change, with row-level security, constraints, controlled views, and a trusted context. An arrow
		down the right side reads "harder to bypass". A note below says the lower layers depend less on the model's
		judgment.
	</desc>
	<defs>
		<marker id="d-gl-arrow" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="8" markerHeight="8" orient="auto-start-reverse">
			<path d="M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z" class="dg-arrowhead"></path>
		</marker>
	</defs>

	<text x="12" y="30" class="dg-title">Three guardrail layers, ordered by how hard they are to bypass</text>

	<g class="dg-node dg-guard">
		<rect x="12" y="52" width="568" height="90" rx="10"></rect>
		<text x="296" y="82" text-anchor="middle" class="dg-accent" font-weight="700">Context layer: what the model sees</text>
		<text x="296" y="106" text-anchor="middle" class="dg-sub">relevance &amp; safety classifiers ·</text>
		<text x="296" y="128" text-anchor="middle" class="dg-sub">moderation · rules · source labels</text>
	</g>
	<g class="dg-node dg-guard">
		<rect x="12" y="152" width="568" height="90" rx="10"></rect>
		<text x="296" y="182" text-anchor="middle" class="dg-accent" font-weight="700">Execution layer: what the model does</text>
		<text x="296" y="206" text-anchor="middle" class="dg-sub">tool risk rating · human confirm ·</text>
		<text x="296" y="228" text-anchor="middle" class="dg-sub">PII filter · output validation</text>
	</g>
	<g class="dg-node dg-guard">
		<rect x="12" y="252" width="568" height="90" rx="10"></rect>
		<text x="296" y="282" text-anchor="middle" class="dg-accent" font-weight="700">Data layer: what may change</text>
		<text x="296" y="306" text-anchor="middle" class="dg-sub">row-level security · constraints ·</text>
		<text x="296" y="328" text-anchor="middle" class="dg-sub">controlled views · trusted context</text>
	</g>

	<g class="dg-edge">
		<line x1="696" y1="52" x2="696" y2="340" marker-end="url(#d-gl-arrow)"></line>
		<text x="638" y="192" text-anchor="middle" class="dg-edge-label">harder to</text>
		<text x="638" y="214" text-anchor="middle" class="dg-edge-label">bypass</text>
	</g>

	<g class="dg-node dg-neutral">
		<rect x="12" y="356" width="568" height="62" rx="10"></rect>
		<text x="296" y="382" text-anchor="middle">Lower layers depend less on</text>
		<text x="296" y="404" text-anchor="middle">the model's judgment</text>
	</g>
</svg>
